<title>USA: N.Y. business loans rose $165 mln in Feb 26 week.</title>
<headline>N.Y. business loans rose $165 mln in Feb 26 week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commercial and industrial loans at the six major New York banks, excluding acceptances, rose $165 million to $44,725 million in the week ended February 26, the Federal Reserve Bank of New York said.</p>
<p>Including acceptances, loans rose $185 million to $44,989 million.</p>
<p>Commercial paper outstanding nationally rose $1,695 million to $814,325 million.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
</text>
